    <section style="background: #f0f9ff; border-left: 4px solid #005f8a; padding: 1.5rem; margin-top: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Marine Park Fee Breakdown (2026 Rates)</h2>
      <p style="color: #5c727f; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Zanzibar's marine parks are managed by the Zanzibar Marine Park (ZMP) under the Zanzibar Commission for Tourism. Fees are per person, per day, and are usually included in tour prices by licensed operators. Below is the official 2026 schedule.</p>

      <h3>Menai Bay Conservation Area</h3>
      <p><strong>Fee:</strong> $10 per adult, $5 per child (3–17). <strong>Valid for:</strong> 24 hours from purchase. Covers dolphin tours, snorkeling trips, and glass-bottom boat tours launching from the southwest coast (Kizimkazi, Fumba, Bwejuu).</p>

      <h3>Mnemba Atoll Marine Reserve</h3>
      <p><strong>Fee:</strong> $25 per adult, $15 per child (3–17). <strong>Valid for:</strong> 24 hours. Required for all snorkeling and diving activities around Mnemba Atoll, northeast of Zanzibar Island. Often included in full-day sailing trips.</p>

      <h3>Chumbe Island Coral Park</h3>
      <p><strong>Fee:</strong> $100 per adult, $50 per child (3–17). <strong>Valid for:</strong> 24 hours. Chumbe is a private nature reserve with its own management. Includes guided nature trail, snorkeling with a park ranger, and interpretation center. Day visitors pay the full fee; overnight guests pay a reduced rate.</p>

      <h3>Other Areas</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Chake Chake (Pemba Island): $8 per adult, $4 per child</li>
        <li>Unguja (general island fee, rarely charged directly): included in accommodation levies for some eco-resorts</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Which Tours Include Fees?</h2>
      <p>This is the most common point of confusion for visitors. Here's the rule of thumb:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Safari Blue (Menai Bay):</strong> $10 menai bay fee usually included. Confirm with operator.</li>
        <li><strong>Mnemba snorkeling:</strong> $25 Mnemba fee usually included.</li>
        <li><strong>Chumbe Island day trip:</strong> $100 fee included in the tour price (it's a private park with strict entry control).</li>
        <li><strong>Dhow sunset cruises:</strong> Sometimes include a reduced fee; check individually.</li>
        <li><strong>Kite surfing lessons:</strong> Usually no marine park fee (activity-specific licensing separate).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The #1 Trap: "Fee Not Included"</h2>
      <p>Many budget operators advertise low base prices but <strong>exclude marine park fees</strong>. You'll be asked for cash at the boat or park gate. Amounts quoted vary: $10–20 per person for a half-day tour, $25–50 for a full-day tour. Always ask these two questions before booking:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>"Are all government marine conservation fees included in your published price?"</li>
        <li>"Which specific parks/areas does your tour visit, and what are the respective fees?"</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Our Policy: All Fees Included Upfront</h2>
      <p>At Spice & Sail, transparency is non-negotiable. Every tour price displayed on our website includes all applicable government marine conservation fees. When you book with us, what you see is what you pay—no surprise cash demands at the boat, park gate, or ranger station. We believe the quoted price should be the final price, especially for travelers budgeting their vacation expenses.</p>
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #fef3c7; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
        <h3 style="color: #92400e; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">✅ Verified Inclusions</h3>
        <p style="color: #78350f; line-height: 1.7;">Our published prices for Safari Blue, Mnemba snorkeling, and Chumbe Island day trips all include the full set of applicable marine park fees. We absorb any fee changes to ensure our guests are never caught short.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>How to Budget for Your Zanzibar Boat Trip</h2>
      <p>When planning your marine activities, budget these fees into your overall trip cost:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Half-day safari/dhow trip: $10–15 per person (menai bay fee)</li>
        <li>Full-day sailing excursion: $25–35 per person (menai bay + possible mnemba fee)</li>
        <li>Mnemba Atoll snorkeling: $25–30 per person</li>
        <li>Chumbe Island day visit: $100 per person (often included in the tour price)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you're planning a mixed day of multiple activities, expect to pay $35–50 per person in park fees alone, on top of gear rental, food, and transportation.</p>
