      <h2 style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #065f46; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">How to Verify Your Ticket is Valid</h2>
      <p style="color: #5c727f; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">When you pay a marine park fee, you should receive either:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A digital receipt emailed to you, with a reference number that the boat operator can verify.</li>
        <li>A physical ticket or sticker issued at the park office, with a hologram or security feature.</li>
        <li>A mention in your tour booking confirmation, confirming the fee is included.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you're asked for cash at the boat and don't receive a receipt or ticket, ask for one. Legitimate operators should provide documentation of your fee payment. Without it, you have no proof of payment if questioned by park rangers.</p>
      <p>Remember: fees contribute directly to marine conservation, local community funds, and the upkeep of Zanzibar's world-renowned reefs. Paying the correct fee—and ensuring it's properly documented—helps protect the very reefs you came to see.</p>
    </section>

